{"name":"Sunday Gloves","hex":"#d7bad1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gloves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of glove"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of glove"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunday","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday is the day of the week between Saturday and Monday. Sunday is a day of rest in most Western countries and a part of the weekend. In some Arab countries, Sunday is a weekday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday","wikidata":"Q132"},{"title":"Glove","blocks":[{"text":"A glove is a garment covering the hand, with separate sheaths or openings for each finger including the thumb. Gloves protect and comfort hands against cold or heat, damage by friction, abrasion or chemicals, and disease; or in turn to provide a guard for what a bare hand should not touch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG/330px-Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glove","wikidata":"Q169031"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Pierre